<title>SINGAPORE: SembCorp 1996 net profit falls 25.2 pct.</title>
<headline>SembCorp 1996 net profit falls 25.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in million Singapore dollars unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		 30.07   vs    40.19</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct		     3.0    vs     3.0</p>
<p>    Group shares (cent)	    13.6    vs    18.1</p>
<p>    Turnover (bln)		   1.50    vs     1.20</p>
<p>    Investment income		1.77    vs     3.81</p>
<p>    Other income		    11.44    vs    11.05</p>
<p>    Operating pretax	     110.91    vs    92.29</p>
<p>    Interest expense		19.10    vs     8.38</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation   63.42    vs    49.74</p>
<p>    Associates			66.47    vs    55.82</p>
<p>    Pretax			    94.86    vs    89.99</p>
<p>    Tax				 54.06    vs    38.26</p>
<p>    Minorities		     (10.74)   vs   (11.53)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		  0.13    vs    14.97</p>
<p>    Dividend pay/register	 June 27/June 13</p>
<p>Note -- SembCorp Ltd said it was finalising a proposed merger of its shiprepair business with Jurong Shipyard Ltd.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
